<BaseLayout title="Suspension and steering">
  <h1>Suspension and steering</h1>
  <p>This page explains the major suspension and steering areas on the third-generation S60 and helps organize inspection notes. It does not provide a VIN-specific parts diagram, alignment specification, or repair procedure. Chassis tuning and hardware can differ by trim, package, wheel size, and Polestar Engineered specification.</p>
  <figure class="diagram">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 720 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="chassis-title chassis-desc">
      <title id="chassis-title">Simplified suspension and steering inspection map</title>
      <desc id="chassis-desc">Conceptual front and rear axle layout identifying wheels, suspension assemblies, steering linkage at the front, and rear suspension links.</desc>
      <g fill="#eaf2fa" stroke="#07569a" stroke-width="2">
        <rect x="92" y="48" width="536" height="64" rx="8"/>
        <rect x="92" y="190" width="536" height="64" rx="8"/>
      </g>
      <g fill="#082d55" font-size="16" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">
        <text x="360" y="86">FRONT AXLE</text><text x="360" y="228">REAR AXLE</text>
      </g>
      <g stroke="#082d55" stroke-width="3" fill="none">
        <path d="M150 80 H245 M475 80 H570 M150 222 H245 M475 222 H570"/>
        <path d="M245 80 L290 130 L430 130 L475 80 M245 222 L290 170 L430 170 L475 222"/>
        <path d="M360 112 V190"/>
      </g>
      <g fill="#ffcf00" stroke="#082d55" stroke-width="2">
